+
+FINDINGS:
+
+NONE blocking.
+
+Notes (no fix required):
+1. `src/llama-model.cpp:1798` discards the return of `ggml_backend_alloc_plan_add()`. Safe: a census allocation
+   failure sets `plan->failed` and `commit()` at `ggml-alloc.c` refuses on it (`if (plan == NULL || plan->failed ...)`),
+   so the loader still throws at line 1801. A group that legitimately returns false (meta buft, empty context)
+   falls through `plan_alloc()` to the ordinary path. Behaviour is correct; only the diagnostic is generic.
+2. Receipt `32-heapres-final.txt` was produced with the WinLibs `mingw64/bin` on PATH. Without it the binary exits
+   rc 127 (missing DLL) on this rig; with it, rc 0 reproduced. Environment fact, already disclosed in report §5.
+
+CHECKED:
+
+1. Production wiring. `src/llama-model.cpp:1762` creates the transaction; census pass 1790-1799 adds every
+   `ml.ctx_map` group that the allocation loop would send to `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft` (same
+   predicates via shared lambdas `resolve_dev` 1769, `uses_host_ptr_path` 1780, plus the same
+   `ggml_get_first_tensor == nullptr` / `ml.no_alloc` skips as lines 1810/1845). `commit()` at 1800 runs before the
+   allocation loop at 1805; the real-buffer call at 1852 is `ggml_backend_alloc_plan_alloc()`. Not a test-only path.
+2. commit() semantics (`ggml-alloc.c`, `ggml_backend_alloc_plan_commit`): overflow check per group before any
+   `plan_begin`; one `ggml_backend_buft_plan_begin` per buffer type with all groups concatenated in add order;
+   `INFEASIBLE` or `INDETERMINATE && n_entries > 1` releases every opened plan and returns false; states flip to
+   RESERVED only after every plan opened. UNSUPPORTED / lone-INDETERMINATE leave `plan == NULL`, unplanned path.
+3. Ownership states explicit: enum `ALLOC_PLAN_GROUP_{CENSUSED,RESERVED,CONSUMED}`; CONSUMED set only after
+   non-NULL buffer from `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_ranges_alloc`. On mid-group failure `alloc_tensor_range` frees
+   built buffers (adopted entries released with them, `ggml-alloc.c:1137-1150`), group stays RESERVED, `free()`
+   releases the rest. `release_plans()` NULLs each plan pointer, so commit-failure path plus `free()` cannot
+   double-free. Loader holds plan in `unique_ptr` with deleter (1759-1762): every throw between commit and last
+   alloc releases unconsumed reservations.
+4. Re-census guard in `plan_alloc()` compares range count, byte total, and first/last/size per range before
+   consuming; refuses on mismatch.
+5. Identity: transaction keys groups by `(ctx, buft)` pointer and plans by buft pointer only; device / memory
+   type / heap index never interpreted in ggml-alloc.c. `git diff --stat` on `ggml-vulkan.cpp`, `ggml-backend.cpp`,
+   `ggml-backend-impl.h` is empty, so the B7a ledger, `reserve_plan()` under `std::lock_guard` (ggml-vulkan.cpp:1115),
+   and `VK_PLAN_MAX_SEARCH_NODES 1000000` (line 1015, checked at 1164) are the accepted inherited code.
+   Concurrent transactions serialise per device ledger; two-transaction over-admission covered by
+   `test_loader_transaction_competing_and_isolated` part 1.
+6. Non-Vulkan / single-buffer / mixed: `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft_impl` now calls
+   `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_ranges` + `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_ranges_alloc(plan_base=0)`; the INDETERMINATE
+   single-buffer fall-through, `no_alloc` early return, `n_buffers == 0` NULL return and multi-buffer wrap are
+   preserved. `alloc_tensor_range` with `plan == NULL` still calls `ggml_backend_buft_alloc_buffer`. Mixed load
+   covered by `test_loader_transaction_mixed_backends` (unplanned buft: `plan_begin_calls == 0`, allocs unchanged;
+   never-joined group falls through). Older 15 test-alloc cases unchanged and passing.
+7. Tests present for every mandated class: later-group infeasibility with zero earlier allocations
+   (`refuses_before_any_allocation`, A first, `alloc_calls == 0`), competing transactions and two-device isolation
+   (`competing_and_isolated`), deterministic assignment and single plan across contexts
+   (`two_contexts_one_buffer_type`, order `0..5`, `plan_free_calls == 1`), mid-load rollback with exact-once
+   discharge (`mid_load_failure_rolls_back`, `reserved == 0`, `released == 2*chunk`), mixed/unsupported
+   (`mixed_backends`), overflow before any `plan_begin` (`overflow_is_refused`). Dummy seam asserts
+   `!plan->consumed[i]` and `plan->reserved == 0` at `plan_free`.
+8. Planted reds: `plant-reds.py` anchors match exactly once, each red built and run alone; receipts
+   `2a..2e-red-*.rc` all `3221226505` (0xC0000409 abort); named failing assertions in `2a..2e-red-*.txt` match the
+   report table (test-alloc.cpp:839, :128, :875, :151, :1034). `29-red-revert-identity.txt` sha256 before == after
