+Goal: close B7b at loader scope. Before the first Vulkan buffer-type/context group for one model load allocates driver memory, gather every intended Vulkan allocation group that this load will request, create their backend batch plans, and atomically decide/reserve the complete cross-group transaction. If any group is infeasible or indeterminate, fail before the first plan-owned driver allocation. On later failure, roll back all unconsumed groups and destroy/release any constructed groups exactly once.
+
+Requirements:
+1. Use the real llama model loader path. Do not add an unused helper or test-only orchestration path.
+2. Preserve the accepted per-buffer-type planner and B7a ledger invariants.
+3. Coordinate multiple buffer types/contexts/devices without conflating device identity, type index, or heap index. Concurrent loader transactions must not over-admit.
+4. Use actual per-group Vulkan requirements already exposed by the versioned backend plan API. Avoid creating driver buffers twice solely to plan.
+5. Define explicit ownership states: planned/reserved, consumed into buffer, rolled back, destroyed. Exceptions at every transition must be safe.
+6. Unsupported non-Vulkan backends and ordinary single-buffer callers retain current behavior. Mixed-backend model loads plan the Vulkan subset as one transaction while leaving nonparticipating backends semantically unchanged.
+7. Add focused production-boundary tests proving: later-group infeasibility yields zero Vulkan driver allocations across earlier groups; cross-group competing transactions; multi-device isolation; mid-load failure rollback; exact-once adoption/release; unsupported/mixed backend behavior; overflow; deterministic assignment. Include meaningful planted reds and restore byte-identically.
+8. Validate with builds and backend correctness tests. A load-only or quality/correctness model cell is permitted if needed to prove the real loader boundary, but it must not record or compare timing, latency, throughput, bandwidth, tokens/sec, or tuning. Do not run llama-bench, performance grids, served A/B, or measurement-window work. If a model-load cell would consume substantial GPU/system resources, leave the command for HQ rather than launching it inside the maker.
+9. B7c bounded host splitting and staging reserve remain explicitly open. Do not implement or claim them here.
+
+Touch the narrowest loader/backend/Vulkan/test files required. Explain every file. No commit, upstream operation, main move, tag, or promotion. Do not read prior huge trace logs. Keep receipts compact under r46b-b7b-loader-evidence/.
+
+Write OPUS-R46-B7B-LOADER-REPORT.md with inherited SHA, production call chain, transaction/ownership proof, changed files, exact commands and rc receipts, planted reds, final hashes, coverage limits, and the exact HQ load-only correctness command if one remains. End exactly PHASE-R46-B7B-LOADER-DONE only when implementation and non-model correctness gates are green. Otherwise end BLOCKED with one precise reason and leave a buildable, plant-free tree.
