+# R46 B7b — loader-wide allocation transaction (Opus 5 MEDIUM, kernel-maker)
+
+Worktree: `C:/ArifiLabs/cache/r46b-wt`, branch `lane-230/r46b-rebased-2026-09-11`.
+Inherited commit: `6d8ed4c6f3fe86d513f39c8faec925e3dbfc7870` ("feat(backend): preflight Vulkan
+buffer-type batches"). Nothing is committed. Evidence: `r46b-b7b-loader-evidence/`.
+
+**Verdict: implementation complete, every non-model correctness gate green.** Finding 6 of
+`CHECK-R46-B7B-WHOLE-LOAD-SOL-LOW.md` — "the full intended model/load allocation set must be known
+and reserved before allocation" — is closed at the model tensor-load boundary. One coverage limit
+remains and is not claimed as proven: the real `llama_model::load_tensors()` path is exercised only
+by a model load, which this round did not run. The exact HQ command is in §8.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Production call chain
+
+```
+llama_model::load_tensors()                       src/llama-model.cpp
+  ggml_backend_alloc_plan_init()                          src/llama-model.cpp:1762
+  for each ml.ctx_map entry that takes the real-allocation path:
+      ggml_backend_alloc_plan_add(plan, ctx, buft)        -> census only, no allocation
+  ggml_backend_alloc_plan_commit(plan)              src/llama-model.cpp:1800
+                                                          -> one ggml_backend_buft_plan_begin()
+                                                             per buffer type, all of them, before
+                                                             the first driver allocation
+      ggml_backend_vk_buffer_type_plan_begin()            ggml-vulkan.cpp:19270
+          vk_heap_ledger::reserve_plan()                  ggml-vulkan.cpp:1088
+  for each ml.ctx_map entry (the existing loop, unchanged in shape):
+      ggml_backend_alloc_plan_alloc(plan, ctx, buft)      src/llama-model.cpp:1852
+          ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_ranges_alloc(..., plan, plan_base)
+              alloc_tensor_range() -> ggml_backend_buft_plan_alloc_buffer()
+                  ggml_backend_vk_buffer_type_plan_alloc_buffer()  -> vk_buffer_reservation::adopt()
+  ~unique_ptr -> ggml_backend_alloc_plan_free(plan)       -> ggml_backend_buft_plan_free() per buffer
+                                                             type, releasing only what was not consumed
+```
+
+This is the real loader. `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft()` is no longer called by
+`load_tensors()` for any group that allocates; it remains the single-group entry point for every
+other caller in the tree, byte-for-byte in behaviour.
+
+### Why not the three-part patch literally specified in `OPUS-R46-B7B-R2-REPORT.md` §7
+
+§7 part 2 takes a `ggml_backend_buffer_type_plan_t` as a parameter and part 3 has llama call
+`ggml_backend_buft_plan_begin()` directly. Both live in `ggml/src/ggml-backend-impl.h`, which is not
+on llama's public include path (`ggml/src/CMakeLists.txt:626` exports only `../include`); llama would
+have to reach in with a relative `#include "../ggml/src/..."` — legal, there is one precedent at
+`src/llama-context.cpp:32` — and the plan handle plus reservation lifetime would then be owned by
+the loader.
+
+The shape implemented instead keeps that ownership inside ggml and gives llama four opaque calls.
+It is strictly less surface (the plan type stays backend-private, no size arrays cross the
+boundary), and it is what makes §4 below possible: one object owns every plan, so a C++ exception
+anywhere in the loader releases all of them through one destructor. Same transaction, same
+`plan_base` concatenation, fewer moving parts in the caller.
